# INDEX.plan

PROJECT
OmniGrid: modular C++20 3D voxel sandbox. SDL3 owns window/input; OgreNext
renders; JSON/Lua own content/worldgen; Jolt physics is planned.

WORKING AGREEMENT
The binding agent contract is AGENTS_OMNIGRID_PRIMUS_IMPETUS.md (milestone
rules, definition of done, forbidden paths, hard stop conditions, GitHub
workflow). This plan is the session-start summary of that contract.

READ FIRST ON EVERY AGENT RUN (Primus-impetus order)
1. INDEX.plan
2. AGENTS_OMNIGRID_PRIMUS_IMPETUS.md (working agreement)
3. docs/STATUS.md
4. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
5. docs/DECISIONS.md
6. docs/MILESTONES.md
7. relevant domain docs (COORDINATES, DYNAMIC_SPACE, WORLDGEN, ...)
8. graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md (if present)
9. git status
10. git log --oneline -10
11. git diff / git diff --cached
12. current GitHub issue + its dependencies (master tracker: #15)

BUILD
Preferred gate: `./compile.sh`
Architecture only: `python3 tools/architecture_check.py --root .`
Static analysis only: `./compile.sh --analyze-only` (architecture + clang-tidy AST)
Headless dependency-light validation: configure with `-DOMNIGRID_BUILD_APP=OFF`.
Do not install/modify OS packages from an autonomous coding run.

TWO ANALYSIS LEVELS
- graphify (graphify-out/): code/architecture knowledge graph. Use
  `graphify query` / `graphify path` / `graphify explain` before larger changes;
  run `graphify update .` after code changes, and `/graphify . --update`
  (via OpenCode) after docs/config/schema changes.
- clang-tidy / C++ AST (`./compile.sh --analyze-only`): the mandatory C++ AST/
  semantic gate. `tools/architecture_check.py` is the deterministic include/
  dependency gate and always runs.
Graphify green does NOT replace clang-tidy green, and vice versa. Neither
replaces the architecture checker.

PHASE-2 COORDINATE INVARIANTS
- Persistent world identity is Sector -> Region -> Section -> ChunkGroup -> Chunk -> Block.
- Default radices: Sector signed int64; Regions/Sector=9e18; Sections/Region=9e18;
  Groups/Section=256; Chunks/Group=16; Blocks/Chunk=16.
- A Section is 65,536 blocks per axis but is a logical sparse locality tier.
- Never flatten global Block/Chunk/Group/Section coordinates into one integer or double.
- Carry/borrow is checked digit-by-digit and outer Sector overflow never wraps.
- Worldgen, chunk storage, streaming and meshing use the hierarchical integer world only.
- Dynamic float objects use `spatial.dynamic`, not world coordinates directly.
- `spatial.bridge.WorldDynamicBridge` is the explicit world <-> DynamicSpace boundary.
- Default DynamicSpace edge is 65,536 blocks and is independent of Section radix.
- Player/NPC/vehicle/future Jolt bodies in one active island must share one DynamicSpace
  and receive rebases transactionally.
- Jolt active simulation radius is independent from DynamicSpace edge.
- Ogre render anchor is independent and may rebase much more frequently.
- ChunkGroup != Jolt PhysicsSystem.

OTHER ARCHITECTURE INVARIANTS
- SDL3 owns native window/event polling. No SDL_Renderer.
- OgreNext is the only renderer.
- Chunks are cubic 3D chunks; X/Y/Z are equal peers.
- ChunkGroups are sparse materialized containers, never dense super-world slabs.
- AIR runtime id 0 does not mean unloaded chunk.
- Worldgen remains deterministic and data-driven.
- No concrete geology/material semantics in generic WorldGen C++.
- No second world-state/event/persistence/construction path; no direct UI/input
  -> ChunkManager::setBlock(); no ECS entity per normal voxel (see
  AGENTS_OMNIGRID_PRIMUS_IMPETUS.md section 0).

MANDATORY END-OF-RUN GATE
- `python3 tools/architecture_check.py --root .`
- normal completion: `./compile.sh` when target system dependencies are present
- never claim the graphical target built if SDL3/OgreNext were unavailable
- never install missing system dependencies automatically
- graphify updated after relevant changes (`graphify update .`, `/graphify . --update`)
- every milestone committed and documented on GitHub (see working agreement)

MILESTONE ROADMAP
See docs/MILESTONES.md. Main sequence: M00 agent/docs baseline -> M01 rename (#14)
-> M02 worldgen baseline (#8) -> M03 contracts/prototypes (#3) -> M04 sidecars (#3)
-> M05 unified world state (#3) -> M06 minimal actions + player interaction (#3/#18)
-> M07 events + Lua callback cache (#3/#7) -> M08 enTT hot state (#3) -> M09 RocksDB
persistence (#3) -> M10 embedded client/server (#13) -> M11 construction foundation (#16)
-> M12 construction blueprints (#17). Parallel lanes (when prerequisites are met):
#4 render/LOD, #6 UI/RmlUi, #9 audio, #10 celestial, #11 vegetation, #12 fluids,
#5 villages.

IMPORTANT FILES
src/world/coordinates/*                 exact hierarchical block world
src/spatial/dynamic/*                   local float DynamicSpace
src/spatial/bridge/*                    only world/dynamic translation boundary
src/camera/*                            DynamicSpace-local free camera
src/world/worldgen/*                    generic Lua field/pass worldgen runtime
src/world/chunk/*                       sparse chunks/groups + streaming
src/render/*                            Ogre-local rendering
src/app/Application.*                   subsystem wiring/rebase transaction
tools/architecture_rules.json           dependency firewall
AGENTS_OMNIGRID_PRIMUS_IMPETUS.md       binding agent working agreement

docs/COORDINATES.md                     Phase-2 world hierarchy
docs/DYNAMIC_SPACE.md                    player/NPC/Jolt local float model
docs/PHASE2_VALIDATION.md                validation and compatibility notes
